Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> program
Rule 1     program -> query SEMICOLON
Rule 2     query -> SELECT column_list FROM STRING where_clause
Rule 3     column_list -> STAR
Rule 4     column_list -> ID
Rule 5     column_list -> column_list COMMA ID
Rule 6     where_clause -> <empty>
Rule 7     where_clause -> WHERE condition
Rule 8     condition -> condition AND condition
Rule 9     condition -> condition OR condition
Rule 10    condition -> ID OPERATOR value
Rule 11    value -> STRING
Rule 12    value -> NUMBER

Terminals, with rules where they appear

AND                  : 8
COMMA                : 5
FROM                 : 2
ID                   : 4 5 10
NUMBER               : 12
OPERATOR             : 10
OR                   : 9
SELECT               : 2
SEMICOLON            : 1
STAR                 : 3
STRING               : 2 11
WHERE                : 7
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

column_list          : 2 5
condition            : 7 8 8 9 9
program              : 0
query                : 1
value                : 10
where_clause         : 2

Parsing method: LALR

state 0

    (0) S' -> . program
    (1) program -> . query SEMICOLON
    (2) query -> . SELECT column_list FROM STRING where_clause

    SELECT          shift and go to state 3

    program                        shift and go to state 1
    query                          shift and go to state 2

state 1

    (0) S' -> program .



state 2

    (1) program -> query . SEMICOLON

    SEMICOLON       shift and go to state 4


state 3

    (2) query -> SELECT . column_list FROM STRING where_clause
    (3) column_list -> . STAR
    (4) column_list -> . ID
    (5) column_list -> . column_list COMMA ID

